  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Asir (Captive) is the first collection of poems by Iranian poet Forugh Farrokhzad originally published in Iran in 1955. This Rhombus Press edition presents to a new generation of Iranians, as well as a new audience of English speakers, a facsimile of the extremely rare first edition/first printing, accompanied by an English translation. [The edition] ... includes 41 poems, an introduction by Shojaeddin Shafa, a clarification by Farrokhzad and 11 illustrations ... The English translation by Farzaneh Milani also includes a translator's note and a 1954 article from Iranian literary magazine Roshanfekr (the Intellectual)"--Publisher's website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Introduction -- Fugitive -- Captive -- The kiss -- Invitation -- The stranger -- Whore -- Farewell -- Memories -- A dream -- Place from the past -- Regret -- Autumn -- Blood and wine -- To the stars -- A bitter encounter -- Missing -- Addressing God -- Lost love -- Runaway flame -- Fleeing in pain -- Rebellion -- Revenge -- Weary -- Forgotten -- Unknown -- Night and desire -- the guest -- Hidden shape -- Return -- The sick one -- Battle cry -- Waiting -- Deserted house -- A bitter tale -- Maiden and spring -- Night monster -- My secret -- Wedding band -- One night -- Broken mirror -- To my sister -- Clarification -- Translator's note -- Reckless poet -- Sin.</subfield>
  </datafield>
